From 9e610a94ad90a84ea127f6a2cafaf5705c97167c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stefan <46031448+StefanPetersTM@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 16:22:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] gnb: add opt-in phone primer compatibility path

CP2985 and CP3114 require explicit private-lab scheduler, HARQ, SR/CSI, user-plane container, and release-lifecycle accommodations before the OCUDU handoff. These are known workarounds, including duplicate reactive downlink transmission and bounded follow-up UL grants; all remain disabled by default.
